# Repo-root ./.env for the STAGING droplet (gitignored).
#
# The deploy workflow copies this into place on every run, so the droplet's
# .env cannot drift, go missing or name another environment. You should not
# need to place it by hand; if you are setting up a box before its first
# deploy, `cp deploy/env.staging.example .env`.
#
# COMPOSE_FILE makes `docker compose <anything>` resolve to base + staging
# overlay on this host, so the deploy workflow and a human debugging over SSH
# type the same commands they would on production. Without it, a bare
# `docker compose up` would start the base alone, which start.sh refuses to
# boot (no RETINA_ENV).
#
# Application secrets and per-host tuning do NOT belong here — they live in
# backend/.env, which both services load via `env_file`.
COMPOSE_FILE=docker-compose.yml:docker-compose.staging.yml
